---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ReferenceFigure from '../components/ReferenceFigure.astro';
import SourceReferences from '../components/SourceReferences.astro';
import references from '../data/references.json';
import media from '../data/reference-media.json';
import { href } from '../lib/site';
const source = (id: string) => references.find(item => item.id === id)!;
const selections = [
  {id:'sisterly-love-2020',title:'Sisterly Love 姐妹情深',details:'2020 · Oil on canvas · 71 × 77 cm',host:'Daiichi Art'},
  {id:'happy-together-2019',title:'Happy Together 欢乐在一起',details:'2019 · Oil on canvas · 71 × 77 cm',host:'Daiichi Art'},
  {id:'three-sisters',title:'Three Sisters',details:'Oil on canvas · 92 × 86 cm',host:'ArtSafe, Singapore'},
];
---
<Base title="Collections & Galleries" description="Explore Keng Seng Choo’s paintings through museum records, external gallery collections and dated auction catalogues, with credited artwork images and original source links." pageType="CollectionPage">
  <article class="wrap collections-page">
    <header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">COLLECTIONS &amp; GALLERIES · <span lang="zh">机构与画廊记录</span></p><h1>Beyond the studio.</h1><p>Discover more of Keng Seng Choo’s work through museums, galleries and published catalogues. Follow each reference to see the original record.</p><p lang="zh">从美术馆图录、画廊作品页与历年拍卖记录，进一步认识龚明金的创作。</p><nav class="section-jumps" aria-label="Collections sections"><a href="#museums">Museum &amp; exhibition records</a><a href="#galleries">Works on gallery websites</a><a href="#catalogues">Auction archive</a></nav></header>
    <section class="institution-feature" id="museums">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">AN INSTITUTIONAL PERSPECTIVE</p><h2>Bank Negara Malaysia</h2><div class="prose"><p>The museum’s <a href={source('bnm-colour').url}><em>Drops of Colour</em></a> exhibition names Keng Seng Choo among artists represented in the Bank’s collection. Its <a href={source('bnm-fishing').url}><em>Keringat</em> online catalogue</a> also discusses his watercolour <em>Fishing Village</em>.</p><p>The coastal scene offers another view of an artist whose practice spans figures, pigeons, batik and watercolour.</p></div><a class="text-link" href={href('/articles/fishing-village-bank-negara-keringat/')}>Read about Fishing Village</a></div>
      <ReferenceFigure id="bnm-fishing-village" alt="Fishing Village by Keng Seng Choo, a pale watercolour of a coastal settlement and boats" />
    </section>
    <section class="section"><div class="story-links"><a href={href('/articles/maybank-of-moments-and-memories-2019/')}><span class="eyebrow">MAYBANK FOUNDATION · 2019</span><strong>Of Moments and Memories</strong><span>A watercolour exhibition catalogue documenting Kampung Nelayan, 1992.</span></a><a href={href('/articles/taipei-asian-federation-watercolor-1987/')}><span class="eyebrow">TAIPEI FINE ARTS MUSEUM · 1987</span><strong>An international exhibition record</strong><span>The museum archive names him in the Asian Federation of Watercolor exhibition.</span></a></div></section>
    <section class="prose"><h2>A further collection reference</h2><p>The contents of <a href={href('/articles/penang-state-art-gallery-collection-catalogue/')}><em>Penang State Art Gallery permanent collection 1965–2011</em></a> also list Keng Seng Choo. National Gallery Singapore’s library records the book; its catalogue entry does not identify his painting or an acquisition date.</p></section>
    <section class="section" id="galleries"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">EXPLORE WORKS ELSEWHERE</p><h2>On gallery websites</h2></div></div><p class="exhibition-intro">A selection of paintings illustrated on external gallery and art-service websites. Titles and recorded details follow the linked hosts; these references do not confirm current representation or availability.</p>
      <div class="external-art-grid">{selections.map(work => {
        const item = media.find(item => item.id === work.id)!;
        return <figure class="external-artwork"><a class="external-art-image" href={item.artworkPage || item.sourcePage}><img src={href(item.image)} width={item.width} height={item.height} loading="lazy" alt={`${work.title} — painting by Keng Seng Choo`} /></a><figcaption><h3>{work.title}</h3><p>{work.details}</p><p class="image-credit">Artwork: Keng Seng Choo · Image source: {work.host}</p><a class="text-link" href={item.artworkPage || item.sourcePage}>View at {work.host}</a></figcaption></figure>;
      })}</div>
      <div class="gallery-directory"><div><h3>Daiichi Art</h3><p>Artist biography and a collection of paintings across different periods.</p><a href={source('daiichi').url}>Explore the artist’s collection at Daiichi Art</a></div><div><h3>ArtSafe, Singapore</h3><p>An artist profile illustrating oil paintings, including <em>Three Sisters</em> and <em>Mother and Daughter</em>.</p><a href={source('artsafe').url}>Read the ArtSafe profile</a></div><div><h3>Younie Gallery</h3><p>A bilingual biography, career history and exhibition archive.</p><a href={source('younie-artist').url}>Read the Younie Gallery profile</a></div></div>
    </section>
    <section class="recognition-panel" id="catalogues"><p class="eyebrow">DATED ARTWORK RECORDS</p><h2>Auction archive</h2><div class="prose"><p>Public catalogues help document earlier works and their recorded media. They are historical references; catalogue estimates and results are not current valuations.</p><ul><li><a href={source('henry-1970').url}><em>Untitled</em>, 1970</a> — batik, 46 × 72 cm; recorded by Henry Butcher for its 17 April 2016 auction.</li><li><a href={source('klas-1973').url}><em>Basket Carriers</em>, 1973</a> — batik, 58 × 36 cm; recorded by KL Lifestyle Art Space for 4 February 2024.</li><li><a href={href('/articles/wells-chinese-catalogue-1980-work/')}>1980 work, Wells lot 071</a> — a Chinese-language catalogue record from 20 August 2023, with the original illustration.</li></ul></div></section>
    <SourceReferences ids={['bnm-fishing','bnm-colour','maybank-2019','daiichi','artsafe','younie-artist','henry-1970','klas-1973']} />
    <footer class="article-end"><a class="button" href={href('/works/')}>Explore the artist’s own archive</a><a class="text-link" href={href('/contact/')}>Contact</a></footer>
  </article>
</Base>
